Private Verification Architecture
MingleLife Identity, Verification and Realm Assignment System
Version: 1.0 Draft
Classification: Core Security Architecture
Status: Pre-Implementation

Overview
MingleLife uses a private verification architecture designed to:

Protect user privacy
Support age-appropriate experiences
Prevent unauthorized realm access
Enable Age Progression System (APS) functionality
Reduce exposure of age-related information
Support regulatory compliance
Maintain teen and adult environment separation
Unlike many social platforms, MingleLife does not publicly display a user's age, birth date, birth year, or age category.

Age information is used exclusively for:

Verification
Realm assignment
Safety enforcement
Legal compliance
Age progression
Design Philosophy
The MingleLife verification model follows a simple rule:

The platform needs to know a user's age group.

Other users do not.

Public display of age information is intentionally restricted to minimize privacy risks and prevent users from being targeted based on age.

